<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<rdf:RDF
  xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
  xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
  xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
  xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
  xmlns:rd="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#"
>
  <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand">
    <owl:versionInfo>1.2.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/releases/resource-demand/1.2.0/resource-demand.owl"/>
    <owl:priorVersion rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/releases/resource-demand/1.1.0/resource-demand.owl"/>
    <dcterms:title>SOS resource demand annotations for CWL</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Extension fields for CWL documents that state how the resource demand of a tool grows with its inputs (parametric dependencies), as a static annotation next to the input schema: complexity variables on input parameters, demand expressions in ResourceRequirement. The annotation states only the shape of the dependency (a sum of products of complexity classes); coefficients are not part of it. A complexity variable stands for a Measure of an input: its value, array length or file size, a domain measure such as the pixel count of a raster (see eo-formats), or a derived measure computed by a probe tool. Declare the namespace in a CWL document with $namespaces: {rd: "https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#"}.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <dcterms:publisher>DFG project SOS</dcterms:publisher>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://github.com/dfg-sos/ontologies"/>
  </owl:Ontology>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#appliesToFormat">
    <rdfs:label>applies to format</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>On a rd:Measure subclass: a file format class (from any vocabulary, e.g. eo:Raster) the measure can be taken from, including its subclasses. An input annotated with the measure must declare such a format. A measure without this annotation does not depend on the format.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:AnnotationProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#bigO">
    <rdfs:label>Big O notation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>The complexity class in Big O notation, for display.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:AnnotationProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#growthFunction">
    <rdfs:label>growth function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Representative function g(x) of a complexity class, as an expression in the variable x using +, -, *, /, ** and log (natural logarithm). An estimator fits a * g(x) per factor; this annotation tells it which g to use.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:AnnotationProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#readsContent">
    <rdfs:label>reads content</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>On a rd:Measure subclass: true if taking the measure requires reading the whole file content (every pixel, feature or record), not only its metadata. Such measures cost time proportional to the file and should be taken once per input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
  </owl:AnnotationProperty>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#unit">
    <rdfs:label>unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Unit in which the demand of a demand property is estimated.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:AnnotationProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#complexity">
    <rdfs:label>complexity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A factor in RDF: how the demand grows with the variable (the value in the term mapping), a subclass of rd:ComplexityClass.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#complexityVariables">
    <rdfs:label>complexity variables</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Field of a CWL input parameter: a list of variables that the demand expressions of the tool can refer to. Each item has the keys symbol (a name, unique within the tool, matching [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*), measure (the IRI of a rd:Measure subclass) and, for a rd:DerivedMeasure, probe (path to the probe tool). Example: inputs: {raster: {type: File, format: eo:GeoTIFF, rd:complexityVariables: [{symbol: n, measure: eo:PixelCount}]}}. Do not use id, name, type or format as keys or as symbols (symbols are keys in the demand terms): CWL rewrites them.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#factors">
    <rdfs:label>factors</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A demand term in RDF: the factors that are multiplied to form the term. The term {n: rd:Linear, d: rd:Quadratic} has two factors.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#measure">
    <rdfs:label>measure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Key in a rd:complexityVariables item: which quantity of the parameter the variable stands for, a subclass of rd:Measure.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#probe">
    <rdfs:label>probe</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Key in a rd:complexityVariables item: the CWL CommandLineTool that computes a rd:DerivedMeasure, as a path relative to the annotated document or an absolute IRI. Required for derived measures, not allowed otherwise.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ramDemand">
    <rdfs:label>RAM demand</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Field of a CWL ResourceRequirement: how the peak memory of the tool grows with its complexity variables. A list of terms that are added; each term is a mapping from the symbol of a complexity variable (declared in rd:complexityVariables) to the IRI of a rd:ComplexityClass subclass; the entries of a term are factors that are multiplied. An empty mapping {} is a constant term. Example for O(n + d^2): rd:ramDemand: [{n: rd:Linear}, {d: rd:Quadratic}].</rdfs:comment>
    <rd:unit>MiB (as CWL ramMin)</rd:unit>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#timeDemand">
    <rdfs:label>time demand</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Field of a CWL ResourceRequirement: how the wall-clock time to result of the tool grows with its complexity variables. Same structure as rd:ramDemand. Example for O(n log n * d): rd:timeDemand: [{n: rd:Linearithmic, d: rd:Linear}].</rdfs:comment>
    <rd:unit>seconds (as CWL ToolTimeLimit)</rd:unit>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#symbol">
    <rdfs:label>symbol</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Key in a rd:complexityVariables item: the variable's name, used by the factors of demand terms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#variable">
    <rdfs:label>variable</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A factor in RDF: the symbol of its complexity variable (a key of the term mapping), declared on an input of the same tool.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ArrayLength">
    <rdfs:label>Array length</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Measure"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The number of items of an array parameter.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass">
    <rdfs:label>Complexity class</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>How a demand grows with one complexity variable, in the sense of Big O notation. Referenced by IRI as the complexity of a factor in a demand term.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Constant">
    <rdfs:label>Constant</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The demand does not grow with the variable. States explicitly that a variable was considered and has no effect.</rdfs:comment>
    <rd:bigO>O(1)</rd:bigO>
    <rd:growthFunction>1</rd:growthFunction>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Cubic">
    <rdfs:label>Cubic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass"/>
    <rd:bigO>O(n^3)</rd:bigO>
    <rd:growthFunction>x ** 3</rd:growthFunction>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#DerivedMeasure">
    <rdfs:label>Derived measure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Measure"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A characteristic of the input that cannot be read from its type or format, computed by a probe: a CWL CommandLineTool, referenced with rd:probe, that takes the parameter as input and returns a single number. Domain vocabularies may name derived measures as subclasses of this class.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Exponential">
    <rdfs:label>Exponential</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass"/>
    <rd:bigO>O(2^n)</rd:bigO>
    <rd:growthFunction>2 ** x</rd:growthFunction>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#FileSize">
    <rdfs:label>File size</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Measure"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The size in bytes of a File parameter (CWL File.size), without its secondaryFiles. For an array of Files, the sum of their sizes.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Linear">
    <rdfs:label>Linear</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass"/>
    <rd:bigO>O(n)</rd:bigO>
    <rd:growthFunction>x</rd:growthFunction>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Linearithmic">
    <rdfs:label>Linearithmic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass"/>
    <rd:bigO>O(n log n)</rd:bigO>
    <rd:growthFunction>x * log(x)</rd:growthFunction>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Logarithmic">
    <rdfs:label>Logarithmic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass"/>
    <rd:bigO>O(log n)</rd:bigO>
    <rd:growthFunction>log(x)</rd:growthFunction>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Measure">
    <rdfs:label>Measure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A quantity taken from the value of an input parameter, used as a complexity variable. Measures are referenced by IRI in rd:complexityVariables. Format-specific measures (pixel count, feature count, ...) are defined in domain vocabularies such as eo-formats as subclasses of this class.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Quadratic">
    <rdfs:label>Quadratic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#ComplexityClass"/>
    <rd:bigO>O(n^2)</rd:bigO>
    <rd:growthFunction>x ** 2</rd:growthFunction>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Value">
    <rdfs:label>Value</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://dfg-sos.github.io/ontologies/resource-demand#Measure"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The numeric value of an int, long, float or double parameter.</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:Class>
</rdf:RDF>
